# Example probe script — read-only inspection of the eMMC + CRU.
#
# This is the language reference / template. It has no #AUTO marker,
# so it is NOT part of the compiled-in battery — the run-all sweep
# skips it. To make it run, add an "#AUTO <N>" line (lower N runs
# earlier) and rebuild the diagnostic kernel:
#   scripts/build --probes
# then flash that image (scripts/push-to-usb here, scripts/lab-side/
# flash-sd on the lab laptop), boot, pull the card, and read the
# results with scripts/lab-side/dump-from-sd. (No #WRITES marker → the
# kernel ignores any W lines; this probe cannot change hardware state.)
#
# Language: one command per line. '#' starts a comment. Numbers are
# hex unless a command says otherwise. Commands:
#   R/RH/RB <addr>          read a 32/16/8-bit register
#   W/WH/WB <addr> <val>    write one (needs #WRITES; allowlisted)
#   DUMP <addr> <count>     log <count> consecutive 32-bit words
#   DELAY <n>               busy-wait roughly <n> units
#   EXPECT <addr> <val> <mask>   read, mask, compare; logs PASS/FAIL
#   CALL <name>             run a driver routine: sd_init, emmc_init,
#                           emmc_read0, backup200
#   LOG <text>              echo a marker line into the log

LOG eMMC SDHCI capabilities (base clock, voltages) and version
R 0xFE310040
RH 0xFE3100FE

LOG CRU: eMMC clock gate CLKGATE_CON9, reset SOFTRST_CON7
R 0xFDD20324
R 0xFDD2041C

LOG CRU: CCLK_EMMC source mux CLKSEL_CON28 (bits 14:12 select rate)
R 0xFDD20170

LOG first 16 SDHCI standard registers
DUMP 0xFE310000 16

LOG confirm we are talking to the expected controller (caps value)
EXPECT 0xFE310040 0x226DC881 0xFFFFFFFF

LOG bring the eMMC up and read block 0 (expect rc 0, real word0)
CALL emmc_init
CALL emmc_read0

LOG probe complete
